.TH SIEMSTRESS 1 2026-09-23 "siemstress 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
siemstress \- lightweight SIEM for homelabs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B siemstress
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-db
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B siemstress
collects logs from the local systemd journal, syslog senders on the network, log
files and the Docker or Podman API; normalizes authentication, privilege, account,
audit and firewall events; raises alerts from detection rules; and provides a case
workflow for working those alerts to a close.
.PP
On a packaged install the collector runs as the
.B siemstress
system service. Members of the
.B siemstress
group can use every other command and the dashboards.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Collecting
.TP
.B run
Collect events until stopped. Normally started by systemd.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the installation end to end and explain how to fix any problem.
.SS Investigating
.TP
.B search \fR[\fB\-\-since\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR \fIU\fR] [\fB\-\-ip\fR \fIIP\fR] [\fB\-\-action\fR \fIA\fR] [\fB\-\-grep\fR \fITEXT\fR]
Search stored events. Durations look like
.BR 15m ", " 2h ", " 7d .
.TP
.B stats
Summarize collected events by host, program and action.
.TP
.B hunt \fR[\fB\-\-since\fR \fIDURATION\fR]
Replay stored events through the rules without saving alerts.
.TP
.B rules
List the active detection rules.
.SS Working alerts
.TP
.B alerts \fR[\fB\-\-status\fR \fIunresolved\fR|\fIopen\fR|\fIacknowledged\fR|\fIresolved\fR|\fIall\fR]
List alerts, unresolved by default.
.TP
.B case \fIID\fR
Print an alert's case file as Markdown: handling, evidence, related events and its
activity log.
.TP
.B ack \fIID\fR...
Acknowledge alerts and take ownership of unowned ones.
.TP
.B assign \fIID\fR... [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIUSER\fR]
Assign alerts, to yourself by default.
.TP
.B note \fIID TEXT\fR
Add a note to an alert's activity log.
.TP
.B resolve \fIID\fR... \fB\-\-disposition\fR \fID\fR \fB\-\-action\fR \fIA\fR... \fB\-\-summary\fR \fITEXT\fR
Close alerts. Dispositions:
.BR true\-positive ", " benign\-positive ", " false\-positive ", " undetermined .
Anything left out is asked for when run in a terminal.
.TP
.B reopen \fIID\fR... \fB\-\-reason\fR \fITEXT\fR
Reopen resolved alerts.
.TP
.B report \fR[\fB\-\-since\fR \fIDURATION\fR]
Alert-handling metrics as Markdown: time to acknowledge and resolve, dispositions,
false positives per rule.
.SS Dashboards
.TP
.B gui
Desktop dashboard (package
.BR siemstress\-gui ).
.TP
.B tui
Terminal dashboard, usable over SSH (package
.BR siemstress\-tui ).
.TP
.B notify\-test
Send a test notification through the configured ntfy topic.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/siemstress/config.toml
System configuration: syslog listener and allowed senders, TLS, collection scope,
sources and notifications.
.TP
.I /etc/siemstress/rules/*.toml
Local detection rules; a rule with a built-in rule's id replaces it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/siemstress/events.db
Events, alerts and case activity (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.config/siemstress/config.toml\fR, \fI~/.local/share/siemstress/events.db
Per-user equivalents, used instead when they exist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIEMSTRESS_CONFIG\fR, \fBSIEMSTRESS_DB
Override the configuration file and database locations.
.SH EXAMPLES
Allow a Debian host to send logs, then check the setup:
.PP
.nf
.RS
[syslog]
listen = "0.0.0.0:5514"
udp = false

[syslog.senders]
"192.168.1.40" = "web01"
.RE
.fi
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo systemctl restart siemstress
siemstress doctor
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd-sysusers (8),
.BR rsyslog.conf (5)
.PP
Documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/siemstress/ :
detection coverage, alert handling and the annotated example configuration.
